Package: rodauth-admin
Version: 0.1.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: ruby (>= 1:3.3), ruby-bundler, ruby-dev, build-essential, libssl-dev
Maintainer: Delano Mandelbaum <delano@onetimesecret.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/onetimesecret/rodauth-admin
Description: Admin console for Onetime Secret operator accounts
 A single standalone Puma process serving the Rodauth-backed admin
 console: operator accounts with MFA, account lookup, verb codes and an
 audit trail against the Onetime Secret auth database.
 .
 The service binds loopback only (127.0.0.1:9292) and is reached over an
 SSH tunnel; IPAddressDeny=any in the unit enforces that at the kernel,
 so the sealed database URLs must be IP literals and the authdb address
 is allowed by a per-host drop-in.
 .
 The six secrets (session secret, auth and argon2 secrets, three database
 URLs) are never written to disk in cleartext: they are sealed with
 systemd-creds into /etc/credstore.encrypted and exported into the
 process environment at start by a wrapper. The migration credential is
 prompted for and never sealed onto the host.
 .
 Gems are installed by postinst from the shipped Gemfile.lock into the
 system Ruby's gem directory, with argon2 and puma compiled on the host;
 hence the build-essential and ruby-dev dependencies. Built locally,
 delivered by scp, installed with apt install ./rodauth-admin_*.deb; no
 apt repository.
